---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { GitPullRequest, ScanSearch, Workflow, BookOpen, ShieldAlert } from '@lucide/astro';
const sections = [
  { icon: ScanSearch, title: 'Scanner adapters', text: 'Use a fixed adapter ID and contract version, validate every field, construct an argument array, bound output, preserve raw JSON, normalize provenance, and register statically.' },
  { icon: Workflow, title: 'Workflow capabilities', text: 'Extend typed Go structures and compiler validation first. Add negative tests for unknown fields, cycles, policy bounds, lock stability, and tamper detection.' },
  { icon: BookOpen, title: 'Documentation', text: 'Keep implemented, experimental, and planned behavior distinct. Verify every CLI example against the Cobra source or a locally built binary.' }
];
---
<BaseLayout title="Contributing — Caphe" description="Build Caphe locally, add adapters and workflow capabilities, test changes, and improve the documentation.">
  <article class="contribute"><header><span>Build with evidence</span><h1>Help make security workflows boring—in the best way.</h1><p>Caphe favors explicit contracts, reproducible fixtures, careful claims, and changes that remain useful with inference disabled.</p><a href="https://github.com/andrew-ships-stuff/caphe"><GitPullRequest/> Open the repository</a></header>
    <section><h2>Development setup</h2><div class="code"><pre><code>git clone https://github.com/andrew-ships-stuff/caphe.git
cd caphe
go test ./...
go vet ./...
go build -o caphe ./cmd/caphe
./caphe doctor</code></pre></div><p>Go 1.26 or newer is required for this development snapshot. Scanner binaries are needed only for workflows or integration tests that invoke them.</p></section>
    <section><h2>Where to contribute</h2><div class="cards">{sections.map(({ icon: Icon, title, text }) => <article><Icon/><h3>{title}</h3><p>{text}</p></article>)}</div></section>
    <section class="tests"><h2>Testing expectations</h2><ul><li>Run <code>go test ./...</code>, <code>go vet ./...</code>, and <code>go build ./cmd/caphe</code>.</li><li>Add fixtures that preserve raw tool records and cover malformed, oversized, missing, and partially failing inputs.</li><li>Keep canonical compilation stable across repeated runs; avoid timestamps in lock content.</li><li>For website work, run <code>npm ci</code>, <code>npm run build</code>, and <code>npm run test:links</code> inside <code>website/</code>.</li><li>Do not turn a model hypothesis into a confirmed finding without an independent verification transition.</li></ul></section>
    <section class="security"><ShieldAlert/><div><h2>Security reports</h2><p>The repository does not yet include a dedicated <code>SECURITY.md</code> or published private disclosure channel. Do not open an issue containing exploit details. Open a minimal issue asking the maintainer for a private contact, without sensitive reproduction information.</p></div></section>
    <section><h2>Pull requests and issues</h2><p>Keep changes scoped, explain trust-boundary effects, add tests for behavior and failure modes, and update documentation when public interfaces change. Use <a href="https://github.com/andrew-ships-stuff/caphe/issues">GitHub Issues</a> for reproducible bugs and bounded proposals.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .contribute { width: min(1040px, calc(100% - 2rem)); margin: 0 auto; padding: 7rem 0; }.contribute > header { max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 6rem; }.contribute header > span { color: var(--caphe-accent); font: 700 .72rem ui-monospace, monospace; letter-spacing: .11em; text-transform: uppercase; }.contribute h1 { margin: 1rem 0; font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 5.4rem); line-height: .98; letter-spacing: -.06em; }.contribute header p { color: var(--caphe-muted); font-size: 1.1rem; line-height: 1.7; }.contribute header a { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .55rem; margin-top: 1rem; border-radius: .7rem; background: var(--caphe-accent); color: var(--caphe-accent-ink); padding: .75rem 1rem; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 750; }.contribute section { margin-bottom: 6rem; }.contribute h2 { font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.8rem); letter-spacing: -.04em; }.contribute section > p, .security p { color: var(--caphe-muted); line-height: 1.7; }.code { overflow-x: auto; border: 1px solid var(--caphe-border); border-radius: .9rem; background: #0a0e11; padding: 1.3rem; color: #d9ddd9; }.code pre { margin: 0; }.cards { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: .8rem; }.cards article { border: 1px solid var(--caphe-border); border-radius: .8rem; background: var(--caphe-surface); padding: 1.3rem; }.cards :global(svg), .security > :global(svg) { color: var(--caphe-accent); }.cards h3 { margin-top: 2rem; }.cards p { color: var(--caphe-muted); font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.65; }.tests ul { display: grid; gap: .7rem; color: var(--caphe-muted); line-height: 1.6; }.tests code, .security code { color: var(--caphe-teal); }.security { display: grid; grid-template-columns: auto 1fr; gap: 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--caphe-accent); border-radius: .9rem; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--caphe-accent), transparent 94%); padding: 1.4rem; }.security h2 { margin-top: 0; }.contribute section a { color: var(--caphe-accent); } @media(max-width:760px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}.contribute{padding-top:4rem}}
</style>
